---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Robotics ETFs vs Direct Stocks: Which Exposure Is Right for You';
const desc = 'ETFs, direct stocks, and crypto perps compared for robotics exposure: what you own, how it is verified, access and risk. Built on the Robotics Supply-Chain Intelligence 2026 dataset.';

const etfs = [
  { ticker: 'KOID', kind: 'Equity ETF', focus: 'Robotics and automation equity basket' },
  { ticker: 'BOTZ', kind: 'Equity ETF', focus: 'Robotics and AI equity basket' },
  { ticker: 'IRBO', kind: 'Equity ETF', focus: 'Robotics and AI, broader international basket' },
  { ticker: 'ROBO', kind: 'Equity ETF', focus: 'Robotics and automation equity basket' },
  { ticker: 'LIT', kind: 'Commodity ETF', focus: 'Lithium: the battery input layer' },
  { ticker: 'REMX', kind: 'Commodity ETF', focus: 'Rare earths and strategic minerals' },
  { ticker: 'BATT', kind: 'Commodity ETF', focus: 'Battery metals and materials' },
];

const rows = [
  { dim: 'What you own', etf: 'A basket: diluted exposure to dozens of names', stock: 'One company: concentrated, thesis-driven', perp: 'A leveraged price bet on a reference price, no equity' },
  { dim: 'Verification in our dataset', etf: 'Mapped in the 60-route exposure layer, indirect route', stock: 'Every ticker live-verified (Yahoo Finance / SEC EDGAR), direct route', perp: '232 Hyperliquid perp assets mapped, adjacent route' },
  { dim: 'Access', etf: 'Any standard brokerage account', stock: 'Depends on listing country; the whole point of our tradeability layer', perp: 'Crypto venue; not available or suitable everywhere' },
  { dim: 'Risk shape', etf: 'Index risk, low single-name blowup risk', stock: 'Single-name risk, highest upside if your thesis holds', perp: 'Liquidation risk is real; the Unitree case is documented' },
  { dim: 'Costs', etf: 'Expense ratio plus spread', stock: 'Commission, FX, and possibly a cross-border premium', perp: 'Funding rates and fees; costs compound' },
];

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: 'Robotics exposure routes: ETFs vs direct stocks vs perps',
  description: 'Comparison of three exposure routes to the robotics supply chain, with the ETF and commodity tickers mapped in the Robotics Supply-Chain Intelligence 2026 dataset.',
  url: Astro.url.href,
  dateCreated: '2026-08-30',
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'vhsgreed', url: Astro.site?.toString() },
  distribution: { '@type': 'DataDownload', encodingFormat: 'CSV', contentUrl: 'https://store.vhsgreed.win/l/robotics-supply-chain-database-2026' },
  variableMeasured: `${etfs.length} ETFs, 3 exposure routes`,
  includedInDataCatalog: { '@type': 'DataCatalog', name: 'Robotics Supply-Chain Intelligence 2026' },
};
---
<Base title={title} description={desc}>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Robotics ETFs vs direct stocks: which exposure is right for you</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Same theme, three very different instruments. ETFs dilute and diversify,
        direct stocks concentrate, and crypto perps price what has not listed
        yet. Here is the honest comparison, grounded in the exposure map we
        built and verified.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn btn-accent" href="https://store.vhsgreed.win/l/robotics-supply-chain-database-2026" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-track="gumroad_click">Get the full dataset</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/robotics-stocks/">All countries</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <section class="section-tight">
      <h2>The ETF and commodity layer in our map</h2>
      <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Ticker</th>
              <th>Type</th>
              <th>What it gives you</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {etfs.map((c) => (
              <tr>
                <td><span class="mono">{c.ticker}</span></td>
                <td>{c.kind}</td>
                <td>{c.focus}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
        <small>These are the indirect and commodity routes in our 60-route exposure map.
        Commodity funds (LIT, REMX, BATT) hedge the input layer: lithium, rare earths,
        battery materials.</small>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
      <h2>Head to head</h2>
      <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Dimension</th>
              <th>ETF</th>
              <th>Direct stock</th>
              <th>Crypto perp</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {rows.map((r) => (
              <tr>
                <td><strong>{r.dim}</strong></td>
                <td>{r.etf}</td>
                <td>{r.stock}</td>
                <td>{r.perp}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="prose section-tight" style="max-width: 72ch;">
      <h2>How to choose</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>You want the theme, not a thesis:</strong> ETF. You accept index dilution in exchange for not being wrong about one company.</li>
        <li><strong>You have a view on a specific link in the chain:</strong> direct stock, ideally from a verified list so you know the ticker actually trades where you think it does.</li>
        <li><strong>You want pre-listing price discovery:</strong> perps, with eyes open. Unitree's pre-IPO perps priced it 75% below a +629% open; the instrument works, and the liquidation risk is real.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These are not mutually exclusive: our own exposure map grades every
        route direct, adjacent, or indirect, and most serious positioning uses
        a mix. What the map removes is the guesswork about which ticker is
        real, tradeable, and from where.
      </p>

      <h2>Related pages</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/robotics-stocks/actuator-stocks/">Actuator stocks: the pick-and-shovel play</a></li>
        <li><a href="/robotics-stocks/humanoid-robot-stocks/">Humanoid robot stocks: who makes the bots</a></li>
        <li><a href="/robotics-stocks/unitree-ipo/">Unitree IPO explained: the +629% open</a></li>
        <li><a href="/robotics-stocks/">Robotics stocks by country</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
</Base>
